ck mt-2","children":"Binary Mind"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-2xl md:text-3xl text-muted-foreground font-medium leading-tight max-w-3xl border-l-4 border-orange-500/30 pl-8 py-2","children":"Advaita Vedanta is the philosophical claim that the boundary between \"you\" and the \"universe\" is not a physical wall, but a persistent cognitive superimposition."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid lg:grid-cols-3 gap-12 mb-20","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"lg:col-span-2 space-y-12","children":[["$","section",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-3xl font-display font-bold mb-6","children":"The Non-Dual Equation"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xl text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-6","children":["The word ",["$","strong",null,{"className":"text-foreground","children":"Advaita"}]," literally translates to \"not-two.\" Unlike dualistic systems that posit a fundamental separation between the Creator and the Created, Advaita asserts that ultimate reality is a singular, indivisible continuum of consciousness. In this framework, your individual soul (Atman) is not a \"piece\" of the divine, but is identical to the absolute totality (Brahman)."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xl text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed","children":"This realization is the central goal of the tradition. It suggests that liberation is not something to be \"attained\" in the future, but a recognition of a truth that is already present. We suffer because we fail to recognize this underlying unity, identifying instead with the temporary shells of body, ego, and circumstance."}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"bg-muted/30 rounded-3xl p-10 border border-border/50","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-3xl font-display font-bold mb-6 flex items-center gap-3","children":[["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":24,"height":24,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round"